WEBVTT

00:01.132 --> 00:03.592
Josuke, just how much
longer are you planning on playing?

00:03.718 --> 00:05.594
If you don't turn it off
right this second,

00:05.720 --> 00:07.096
I'm really gonna lose it.

00:07.264 --> 00:09.474
Five more minutes! Please!

00:09.558 --> 00:11.685
Just five more minutes!

00:11.768 --> 00:14.771
The best part is coming up!

00:15.021 --> 00:16.397
If I stop now,

00:16.481 --> 00:19.233
I'll live the rest of my life
a man who can't follow through.

00:19.317 --> 00:21.610
- It'll haunt me till the day I die!
- Okay! The longer you keep playing,

00:21.695 --> 00:24.155
- Is that the kind of son you want, Mom?!
- the harder these kicks are gonna get!

00:24.906 --> 00:26.991
Just how long can you hold out?

00:30.245 --> 00:32.288
That's it…

00:32.789 --> 00:33.498
Shii…

00:33.582 --> 00:35.458
Put it away and
start your homework.

00:35.792 --> 00:38.294
Jesus, you could at least take off
your uniform when you get home.

00:38.420 --> 00:39.546
It's pitch-black out there!

00:47.762 --> 00:49.638
<i>I can't see you anymore.</i>

00:50.265 --> 00:52.976
<i>Why, Sachiko?
You've stopped loving me?</i>

00:53.059 --> 00:54.685
- What the…?
<i>- That's not it.</i>

00:54.769 --> 00:56.645
- I know I turned it off.
<i>- I think I'm gonna leave town.</i>

00:56.771 --> 00:59.523
- Huh? Thing won't work.
<i>- So you're just going to forget about me?</i>

00:59.900 --> 01:03.069
<i>Looks like Jotaro Kujo has
refused to high-tail it out of this town…</i>

01:04.195 --> 01:07.323
<i>And after I went through
all that trouble to warn him.</i>

01:07.949 --> 01:12.449
<i>So, what gives,
Josuke Higashikata?</i>

01:13.455 --> 01:14.581
You're…

01:17.918 --> 01:20.086
Chili Pepper?!

01:35.518 --> 01:37.937
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE
DIAMOND IS UNBREAKABLE

01:39.230 --> 01:42.524
<i>These faceless gazes pass by one another</i>

01:42.901 --> 01:46.195
<i>A wound to the heart changes our everyday</i>

01:46.446 --> 01:50.946
<i>Encounters without boundaries
The bizarre is our normal U-yeh</i>

01:53.411 --> 01:56.747
<i>These ordinary mornings,
we're laughing on the surface</i>

01:56.831 --> 02:00.417
<i>Mysteries drawn to each other,
identity still unknown</i>

02:00.502 --> 02:05.002
<i>Without a heads up,
it's quietly lurking somewhere in this town</i>

02:09.636 --> 02:14.136
<i>Although we bicker and complain
In the end, we celebrate</i>

02:16.685 --> 02:20.063
<i>Dancing through the everyday</i>

02:20.146 --> 02:24.646
<i>Crazy Noisy Bizarre Town</i>

02:36.913 --> 02:41.167
EPISODE 11
CHILI PEPPER, PART 1

02:38.999 --> 02:40.125
What are you doing here?

02:40.333 --> 02:41.188
Missed the boat again, I see.

02:42.502 --> 02:46.464
I've been popping in
off and on for a while now.

02:46.548 --> 02:47.298
<i>What?</i>

02:47.424 --> 02:50.760
<i>So this asshole's been
watching me this entire time!</i>

02:52.262 --> 02:55.265
The house belonging to the brother of
that fool, Keicho, I knocked off,

02:55.390 --> 02:57.809
Okuyasu has been on
my "places to visit" list, too.

02:57.934 --> 03:02.434
I'm also well aware of Yukako Yamagishi
and Koichi Hirose's Reverb.

03:03.231 --> 03:04.941
And I know that Toshikazu Hazamada

03:05.025 --> 03:07.944
and Tamami Kobayashi
are currently hospitalized.

03:08.236 --> 03:10.363
That's why I'm asking.

03:10.572 --> 03:13.324
What is a yellow,
sneaking coward like you

03:13.616 --> 03:18.116
suddenly showing himself
fair and square to a guy like me?

03:18.663 --> 03:19.997
You wouldn't…

03:20.331 --> 03:24.376
be moronic enough to think you could
actually mess me up, would you?

03:24.544 --> 03:26.003
Mess you up?

03:26.087 --> 03:28.923
I'd never put you through
something so unpleasant.

03:29.090 --> 03:31.383
I'm here to administer you
a humane death.

03:32.594 --> 03:35.096
So you're a comedian with
a crappy sense of humor,

03:35.263 --> 03:37.139
I see, sir.

03:38.975 --> 03:41.018
I've told Jotaro myself.

03:41.102 --> 03:44.688
His Star Platinum poses
a great threat to me.

03:44.856 --> 03:46.983
His watchfulness is unwavering,

03:47.108 --> 03:50.611
and Star Platinum's time-stopping ability
is formidable.

03:50.695 --> 03:55.195
As you could guess, I was eager to see
how far my own Stand had evolved.

03:58.244 --> 04:00.037
So, before I fought Jotaro,

04:00.121 --> 04:04.500
I wanted to test my abilities
against you, Josuke Higashikata.

04:05.001 --> 04:07.545
Why don't you come a little bit closer?

04:07.796 --> 04:08.671
Closer!

04:09.130 --> 04:10.881
I want you to be able
to unleash an attack

04:10.965 --> 04:14.843
as speedy and precise
as Star Platinum, Josuke!

04:15.136 --> 04:18.764
Come on! From back there,
your punches won't be quite up to snuff.

04:18.890 --> 04:20.558
Am I detecting mockery?

04:20.642 --> 04:22.268
Not in the slightest.

04:22.393 --> 04:26.230
I just have a firm grasp on
your true capabilities.

04:26.356 --> 04:30.856
Come closer and
give me your best shot.

04:31.861 --> 04:32.653
Here!

04:32.821 --> 04:34.697
Hit me right here, come on!

04:35.073 --> 04:36.657
Scooch on in close.

04:38.535 --> 04:40.745
Huh? H-He's fast…

04:41.162 --> 04:43.664
I'm getting a little tired
of your squawking!

04:45.291 --> 04:47.793
He's faster than I ever imagined!

04:49.879 --> 04:51.881
Keep it up,

04:51.965 --> 04:53.925
and I'll just have to
debeak you myself!

04:54.592 --> 04:55.718
And by the way!

04:55.844 --> 05:00.139
Jotaro's Star Platinum's got
nothing on me!

05:00.306 --> 05:01.598
<i>That was a mistake.</i>

05:01.766 --> 05:05.394
<i>My arrogance got the best of me.
I underestimated his ability.</i>

05:09.732 --> 05:10.482
<i>What?!</i>

05:16.531 --> 05:19.283
Josuke! What's with
all the commotion?

05:19.576 --> 05:20.618
That blow…

05:20.702 --> 05:24.497
That was like being on
the receiving end of a jet-engine blast…

05:25.039 --> 05:27.583
He might be stronger than Mr. Jotaro…

05:27.709 --> 05:29.752
Impressive, Josuke.

05:30.044 --> 05:33.422
Your Shining Diamond is a surprise.

05:33.548 --> 05:36.592
I guess I'm not the only one
who's matured.

05:36.676 --> 05:38.219
It isn't my time yet.

05:38.428 --> 05:42.473
Until Chili Pepper is stronger,

05:42.557 --> 05:44.934
vanquishing Jotaro will remain
an impossibiltiy.

05:48.730 --> 05:51.441
<i>All he needs is
a source of electricity…</i>

05:51.566 --> 05:55.611
<i>He has more than immense strength.
He can control his Stand from faraway.</i>

05:58.615 --> 06:02.035
Josuke, I asked you
what's with all the commotion!

06:02.202 --> 06:04.537
It's nothing.

06:07.665 --> 06:11.168
Dammit, another bug got me!

06:11.377 --> 06:15.047
Son of a…
These things always swarm to me.

06:15.131 --> 06:16.799
Ah, Josuke!

06:17.133 --> 06:18.884
Sorry for the wait.

06:18.968 --> 06:21.387
What is all this about, Josuke?

06:21.512 --> 06:24.848
Why'd you want to meet
out here in the boondocks?

06:24.933 --> 06:28.895
Couldn't we've gone to Tonio's
or that café?

06:29.270 --> 06:31.939
I wasn't the one who called
you guys out here.

06:32.315 --> 06:33.232
It was Jotaro.

06:33.733 --> 06:35.985
Jotaro? Wonder what he wants.

06:36.611 --> 06:38.195
I'm guessing it's about Chili Pepper.

06:38.321 --> 06:40.072
What?! Chili Pepper?

06:40.240 --> 06:42.742
You mean the Stand, Chili Pepper?!

06:48.790 --> 06:50.750
So he's back…

06:51.292 --> 06:54.336
Yeah. He came to my house last night.

06:54.629 --> 06:55.212
You prick!

06:55.296 --> 06:57.006
Why didn't you tell me right away?

06:57.715 --> 06:58.674
<i>Okuyasu…</i>

06:58.967 --> 07:03.467
<i>He turns into a different person
at the slightest mention of Chili Pepper.</i>

07:04.305 --> 07:07.308
<i>How can you blame him?
He lost his brother to that Stand…</i>

07:08.351 --> 07:10.519
I told Josuke to keep quiet.

07:11.437 --> 07:15.524
Discussing this downtown
surrounded by electricity is too risky.

07:16.317 --> 07:17.192
Jotaro!

07:17.277 --> 07:20.613
I had us meet here
to avoid being overheard.

07:21.447 --> 07:25.947
Okuyasu, you should know Chili Pepper
grates the shit outta me, too.

07:26.536 --> 07:29.789
He slithers into people's homes.

07:29.956 --> 07:33.542
He eavesdrops on conversations,
and swipes whatever he wants.

07:34.919 --> 07:38.047
So that's why I woke up
to my homework

07:38.172 --> 07:40.591
being gone from my desk the other day!

07:40.967 --> 07:43.636
I could've sworn my mom
threw it out with the trash—

07:43.720 --> 07:46.973
That's the least of our worries, Koichi!

07:47.473 --> 07:49.975
What I'm saying is the only reason

07:50.184 --> 07:52.811
Chili Pepper hasn't raised even
more hell is 'cause we're around.

07:53.313 --> 07:56.190
With the ease of a dirty pervert
making an intrusive phone call,

07:56.274 --> 08:00.403
he drags anyone who
pisses him off into the phone lines.

08:01.696 --> 08:03.739
No doubt he has use
of the bow and arrow.

08:03.823 --> 08:06.283
Question is who he's shot.

08:06.701 --> 08:09.787
I know first-hand he's stronger now.

08:10.121 --> 08:14.083
We have to find his user fast!

08:15.126 --> 08:16.877
B-But how?

08:17.128 --> 08:20.714
We're here together to
figure that out, right, Mr. Jotaro?

08:20.840 --> 08:22.466
No, not quite.

08:22.717 --> 08:24.677
Believe me, we will track him down.

08:25.053 --> 08:27.013
And the one who's fit for the job

08:27.430 --> 08:30.516
is arriving at
the Port of Morioh at noon today.

08:30.725 --> 08:31.350
Huh?

08:31.434 --> 08:32.643
You know someone who can find him?

08:32.935 --> 08:34.561
Is he a Stand user?!

08:34.896 --> 08:35.771
Uh-huh.

08:35.897 --> 08:38.357
His Stand's is called Hermit Purple.

08:38.566 --> 08:41.151
But he's way too old now.

08:41.652 --> 08:43.570
Fighting's out of the question.

08:44.030 --> 08:46.574
Too old? So how old is this guy?

08:46.908 --> 08:48.618
So you've met this guy before?

08:48.701 --> 08:51.370
Yeah. I know him well.

08:51.454 --> 08:54.039
He used to be quite the beefcake,

08:54.165 --> 08:56.083
though you wouldn't know it today.

08:56.751 --> 08:59.670
He's 80… Or was it 79…

08:59.754 --> 09:02.673
79?! He's ancient history!

09:02.840 --> 09:06.134
His legs definitely aren't what
they used to be, so he's got a cane.

09:06.219 --> 09:08.971
And two years ago
he had gallstones removed,

09:09.097 --> 09:10.473
not to mention he had cataracts, too.

09:11.557 --> 09:13.016
He has nothing but false teeth,

09:13.101 --> 09:15.645
and grumbles about
missing his T-bone steaks.

09:16.062 --> 09:17.563
He's also going senile.

09:17.980 --> 09:19.439
Hey, come on.

09:19.524 --> 09:22.944
Now you're gonna tell me
he likes talking to mailboxes.

09:23.111 --> 09:25.613
Give me a break!

09:25.947 --> 09:29.659
I had you guys come here
so you could protect the Old Man.

09:30.118 --> 09:34.618
If Chili Pepper finds out he's here,
you can bet he'll take him down.

09:35.289 --> 09:39.789
Because the thing Chili Pepper dreads
most is having his user identified.

09:40.294 --> 09:44.673
Yeah, but how is an
old timer like that gonna help us?

09:44.757 --> 09:47.968
I tried to stop him, but as soon as
he heard about the bow and arrow,

09:48.052 --> 09:50.721
he headed to Japan on his own.

09:50.847 --> 09:54.642
To Japan?
Mr. Jotaro, so this fellow isn't Japanese?

09:55.017 --> 09:55.767
Correct.

09:56.102 --> 09:58.062
Josuke, th-this is serious!

09:58.271 --> 10:00.231
Huh? What is?

10:00.314 --> 10:04.651
Josuke! Think about it…
A 79-year-old Stand user not from Japan…

10:05.486 --> 10:07.196
Y-You can't mean…

10:14.245 --> 10:16.121
I heard all I need to hear.

10:16.247 --> 10:17.748
Chili Pepper!

10:17.874 --> 10:20.167
Shit! How'd he get out here?

10:30.553 --> 10:32.513
MORIOH LANDMARK #4
MORIOH GRAND HOTEL
HOW TO GET THERE: FROM TERMINAL #1,
TAKE THE "MORIOH GRAND
SWIMMING AREA" BUS
TO "MORIOH GRAND HOTEL".

10:32.597 --> 10:34.557
SURROUNDED BY EXTRAVAGANT VILLAS,
THE MORIOH GRAND HOTEL OOZES
ELEGANCE AND OLD-WORLD CHARM,
AND FOR YEARS HAS BEEN
THE BELOVED GO-TO SPOT
FOR TRAVELERS TO MORIOH.
BESIDES ITS ACCOMMODATIONS,
THE HOTEL IS KNOWN FOR SERVING
MORIOH BEEF TONGUE TO CROWDS
OF ADORING REGULARS
AND TRAVELERS ALIKE.

10:35.475 --> 10:38.895
Why?! There aren't any
power lines here, so how?!

10:39.020 --> 10:40.187
The motorcycle battery.

10:40.354 --> 10:43.815
Shit! He must've hidden in
the battery and followed us here.

10:44.192 --> 10:45.276
In my motorcycle?

10:45.443 --> 10:46.569
He heard us!

10:46.903 --> 10:48.738
So, the port at noon, eh?

10:48.863 --> 10:52.575
There's an old fogy
Stand user who can find me, huh?

10:53.534 --> 10:58.034
The moment that codger
pulls into port, I'll massacre him!

10:58.539 --> 11:00.249
Now he knows about the old man…

11:01.042 --> 11:03.377
He knows…
about Josuke's father!

11:07.215 --> 11:08.466
This isn't good.

11:08.549 --> 11:11.802
At this rate, he's gonna get
to the old man before we do.

11:12.803 --> 11:16.640
Josuke! We've got to chuck a rock
at that bike and take it down!

11:16.766 --> 11:18.350
Not so fast.

11:19.268 --> 11:23.768
In the name of revenge,
I, Okuyasu Nijimura,

11:25.066 --> 11:26.609
will crush that criminal!

11:26.734 --> 11:28.610
He cut through space!

11:32.323 --> 11:34.366
Ack! Keicho's little brother!

11:34.492 --> 11:37.495
You will fight me now.

11:37.620 --> 11:39.288
I'll scratch you out!

11:41.249 --> 11:44.293
Okuyasu, you have my compliments.

11:44.418 --> 11:48.130
Teleporting yourself here
to the motorcycle was extraordinary.

11:48.381 --> 11:52.468
But that little scratching motion
you do with The Hand

11:52.593 --> 11:57.093
is no match for Chili Pepper's speed.

11:58.391 --> 12:00.142
You're slow!

12:00.268 --> 12:02.270
Take another look, dickhead.

12:02.395 --> 12:04.397
When I said scratch you out,

12:04.564 --> 12:06.649
I meant the motorcycle.

12:07.024 --> 12:08.316
The front wheel!

12:20.955 --> 12:23.374
You won't be escaping anywhere now.

12:23.916 --> 12:27.002
Now that's using your head,
Okuyasu. Bravo!

12:27.295 --> 12:31.549
Chili Pepper can't move
very far from the motocycle battery.

12:32.091 --> 12:33.217
In other words… Look!

12:33.551 --> 12:35.803
The nearest power line is
at least a hundred meters away.

12:36.262 --> 12:38.597
We've got you bagged!

12:38.973 --> 12:40.015
That was close!

12:40.474 --> 12:42.893
We haven't captured him just yet.

12:43.019 --> 12:45.730
The battery's still there.

12:46.063 --> 12:49.691
He'll do whatever it
takes to kill Okuyasu and run.

12:51.527 --> 12:52.528
We're going, too!

12:52.695 --> 12:53.570
- Right!
- Right!

12:54.322 --> 12:56.324
You really think you've cornered me?

12:56.616 --> 12:59.201
This is all to avenge Keicho, eh?

13:00.661 --> 13:01.703
No.

13:01.829 --> 13:03.622
My Bro…

13:04.165 --> 13:06.584
his death was inevitable.

13:06.792 --> 13:09.669
I knew someone would kill him one day.

13:10.504 --> 13:11.963
The thing about crime is…

13:12.340 --> 13:14.717
eventually, after a while,
in someway or another,

13:15.092 --> 13:18.095
it all catches up with you.

13:18.846 --> 13:21.807
That much even I know.

13:24.518 --> 13:26.895
Now about your user…

13:27.021 --> 13:29.523
Tell me who he is
and where he lives,

13:29.690 --> 13:32.693
and I'll spare you your life.

13:33.527 --> 13:37.072
If I tell you,
you'll spare me my life?

13:37.365 --> 13:39.200
You are surprisingly composed.

13:39.575 --> 13:41.451
I was certain the hollow of
your miserable bowels

13:41.535 --> 13:44.287
would have burned with
vengeful fury by now!

13:44.538 --> 13:48.750
Deep down, I was hoping you
wouldn't give me the info on your user!

13:48.876 --> 13:53.338
I'm itching to scrape you away,
you electrified shit head!

13:53.881 --> 13:55.132
There he is.

13:55.216 --> 13:56.926
But you want to scrape me away?

13:57.885 --> 14:00.512
With that tragically slow right hand?

14:02.348 --> 14:05.100
I don't know whether
I should laugh or yawn!

14:05.226 --> 14:07.436
It's a tough choice!

14:07.561 --> 14:08.728
You bastard!

14:09.063 --> 14:10.856
I'll annihilate you!

14:10.981 --> 14:13.149
I'll make sure you truly realize

14:13.275 --> 14:16.778
just how pathetically
sluggish your Stand is!

14:24.286 --> 14:27.580
Do you get it now? You're slow!

14:27.665 --> 14:28.457
Okuyasu!

14:28.582 --> 14:29.624
- Okuyasu!
- Shit!

14:29.917 --> 14:31.126
<i>Here comes Jotaro…</i>

14:31.252 --> 14:33.128
<i>I can't stick around here for long.</i>

14:35.673 --> 14:37.174
<i>What?! He's behind me?!</i>

14:37.758 --> 14:41.803
I may've missed,
but I still swiped away space,

14:41.929 --> 14:44.181
all so I could teleport!

14:44.598 --> 14:46.141
Forget about that?

14:48.769 --> 14:50.270
Got ya!

14:50.855 --> 14:53.023
You beak-nosed freak!

15:05.953 --> 15:09.206
Looks like you're dragging a bit now.

15:09.457 --> 15:12.543
Think you can slip by my next attack?

15:12.835 --> 15:16.213
Look! Chili Pepper's
electric charge is fading!

15:16.505 --> 15:17.255
He's getting weaker!

15:17.381 --> 15:19.800
His Stand power must be running out!

15:20.134 --> 15:22.302
Looks like this is Okuyasu's win!

15:22.470 --> 15:24.180
Okuyasu!
The finishing blow can wait!

15:24.305 --> 15:25.848
Let us get there first.

15:25.973 --> 15:27.349
You've already won!

15:27.475 --> 15:31.520
We've got to get him to tell us
where the bow and arrow are.

15:32.229 --> 15:35.357
You're right…
I am getting weaker.

15:35.524 --> 15:40.024
Your Stand may be pathetically slow,
but its power is downright chilling.

15:42.072 --> 15:43.698
However…

15:44.074 --> 15:47.202
You sure you don't want to
wipe me out for good?

15:48.162 --> 15:52.662
How do you know I'm not pretending
to be frail…

15:53.501 --> 15:55.127
- Okuyasu?
- What?!

15:55.669 --> 15:59.923
Perhaps I'm luring Jotaro
in close to quickly sheer off his head.

16:00.007 --> 16:01.383
What is all this bullshit about?

16:01.509 --> 16:02.676
Oh, nothing.

16:03.010 --> 16:06.054
So what'll it be?
Will you kill me now,

16:06.305 --> 16:08.432
or wait for Jotaro?

16:09.892 --> 16:11.310
You bastard…

16:13.646 --> 16:18.146
Wait a minute.
Why would you tell me all this?

16:18.692 --> 16:20.819
<i>If he hadn't hinted he was acting,</i>

16:21.153 --> 16:25.653
<i>he could've easily played us all,
and taken me and Jotaro out…</i>

16:25.783 --> 16:29.912
<i>Then that means, then…
Since he basically told me he's fine,</i>

16:30.037 --> 16:34.537
<i>then my chance of him
attacking me is zero, right?</i>

16:35.876 --> 16:38.378
So I guess you want me
to kill you, after all!

16:38.546 --> 16:41.257
I'll let you figure that out.

16:42.049 --> 16:44.259
<i>Could he really be at death's door?</i>

16:44.385 --> 16:47.596
<i>Or was it all a lie,
and he's really fine?</i>

16:47.721 --> 16:49.597
<i>Which could it be?</i>

16:51.642 --> 16:54.895
Are you going to do it or aren't you?

16:55.479 --> 16:59.691
<i>If he's not injured,
I have to kill him now.</i>

17:00.025 --> 17:03.945
<i>He could have something up
his sleeve.</i>

17:06.532 --> 17:08.200
Should I?

17:09.201 --> 17:11.328
Okuyasu… Something's wrong.

17:12.997 --> 17:15.833
Make up your mind, Okuyasu.

17:23.591 --> 17:25.301
Dammit!

17:25.426 --> 17:29.805
The hell with everything, goddammit!

17:30.306 --> 17:31.348
Okuyasu!

17:31.432 --> 17:33.767
Don't even think
of stopping me, Jotaro!

17:34.476 --> 17:37.812
He killed Bro!
And I'm gonna finish this!

17:38.480 --> 17:40.732
There's only one truth…

17:41.275 --> 17:44.152
And my heart doesn't lie!

17:44.278 --> 17:47.281
Eat shit and die, shithole!

17:53.454 --> 17:54.288
Well, that's great.

17:54.663 --> 17:57.499
Finding the bow and arrow's
gonna be a real pain now.

17:57.958 --> 18:00.001
So it's settled.

18:00.461 --> 18:02.671
No, something's wrong.

18:02.963 --> 18:06.549
It looks like Chili Pepper
really was plotting something.

18:07.009 --> 18:07.843
Huh?!

18:13.140 --> 18:15.058
<i>Underground electrical cables?</i>

18:15.476 --> 18:18.937
<i>That bastard!
He did all this so I'd expose them!</i>

18:20.314 --> 18:23.358
I really was fading.

18:23.484 --> 18:27.362
That motorcycle battery holds
only 12 volts.

18:27.571 --> 18:30.490
- Goodness, that was close!
- Why, you…

18:32.618 --> 18:35.078
And you were considerate enough
to revive me!

18:36.747 --> 18:38.081
Okuyasu!

18:38.207 --> 18:39.875
If only you'd been a good boy

18:40.042 --> 18:43.003
and controlled yourself
like Jotaro instructed,

18:43.128 --> 18:46.005
I would've faded away
with the battery.

18:46.131 --> 18:46.714
Wha…

18:46.799 --> 18:50.886
I know the location of every
electrical line in this town.

18:50.970 --> 18:54.056
I thought about escaping
into those cables,

18:54.181 --> 18:56.725
but they were too far
from that motorcycle.

18:57.101 --> 19:00.437
And there was no way I had
the strength to dig to the cables.

19:00.521 --> 19:03.482
You bastard!

19:03.816 --> 19:04.942
Now he's even more…

19:05.693 --> 19:09.279
Which means that electricity,
that power…

19:09.363 --> 19:12.115
is now my right hand.

19:26.088 --> 19:28.256
Okuyasu!

19:34.346 --> 19:38.846
I remember your brother Keicho
said you never failed to hold him back.

19:39.727 --> 19:40.978
Now I know he was right.

19:41.228 --> 19:43.772
Your soul is undeveloped.

19:45.399 --> 19:49.319
Revenge was never
in the cards for you, idiot!

19:49.445 --> 19:51.989
Bye-bye, Jotaro, Josuke!

19:52.197 --> 19:54.282
And Joseph Joestar, was it?

19:54.408 --> 19:58.908
I'll make sure that old coot will share
the same fate as the Nijimura Brothers!

19:59.288 --> 20:01.123
I win!

20:01.248 --> 20:03.291
Okuyasu!

20:09.965 --> 20:11.549
He pulled him in!

20:12.593 --> 20:14.303
Okuyasu!

20:14.762 --> 20:16.722
Okuyasu!

20:16.805 --> 20:17.972
Good grief.

20:18.140 --> 20:20.851
To think we were that close,
and he still got away.

20:21.226 --> 20:23.353
That was a pretty scary Stand.

20:23.520 --> 20:26.147
Who'd a thunk: a remote Stand with
the boundless power to tap

20:26.273 --> 20:29.317
- every electrical company within reach.
- What?! What are you guys saying?!

20:29.651 --> 20:32.612
Okuyasu has just been murdered,

20:32.905 --> 20:34.865
and you guys are talking about
how strong the enemy was?!

20:35.908 --> 20:38.660
I suppose you're right.
Guess we should check up on Okuyasu.

20:38.952 --> 20:39.827
Right.

20:40.120 --> 20:41.996
There is one consolation.

20:42.664 --> 20:44.957
Okuyasu must have a guardian angel.

20:45.667 --> 20:49.921
Okuyasu was lucky
his right arm was chopped off.

20:50.089 --> 20:50.756
Huh?

20:50.839 --> 20:52.173
Shining Diamond!

20:54.468 --> 20:58.968
Once I fix his arm,
his body will come back.

21:02.976 --> 21:04.268
Damn it!

21:04.645 --> 21:08.690
Yay! Okuyasu is back!

21:10.526 --> 21:13.862
Shit… I-I…

21:14.446 --> 21:17.532
I was totally outclassed
by that bastard.

21:18.325 --> 21:21.244
Dammit! Dammit!

21:22.788 --> 21:26.041
It's not about getting revenge
or winning or losing.

21:26.834 --> 21:30.379
We have to think about
protecting Joseph Joestar.

21:31.004 --> 21:34.841
That's how we'll defeat Chili Pepper.

21:35.968 --> 21:39.221
You have to… for everyone.

21:39.847 --> 21:42.474
For our town…

21:42.766 --> 21:45.310
Jotaro, this really isn't good.

21:45.602 --> 21:47.562
I guess I took it all too lightly.

21:47.688 --> 21:51.400
Yeah. We have to reach the old
man's boat before Chili Pepper.

21:51.567 --> 21:52.693
We can head to the port now.

21:52.860 --> 21:55.445
Hey, you guys!
How could you be so nonchalant?

21:55.612 --> 21:57.989
Okuyasu's still in shock!

21:58.073 --> 22:00.450
It's faster to the port this way.

22:00.576 --> 22:01.326
All right.

22:01.535 --> 22:03.203
Hey, wait!

22:03.537 --> 22:06.081
I've got to surpass my Bro…

22:06.248 --> 22:09.125
I learned a lot from this,
Chili Pepper.

22:14.798 --> 22:16.174
Mr. Joestar.

22:16.383 --> 22:18.760
We'll be arriving at
the Port of Morioh any moment now.

23:38.966 --> 23:42.052
EPISODE 12
CHILI PEPPER, PART 2
